  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The unit circle extends sine, cosine and tangent to all angles and produces periodic graphs.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Unit circle &amp; graphs",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>On the unit circle a point is \\( (\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta) \\). Radians: \\( 180^{\\circ}=\\pi \\). The graphs of \\( \\sin x \\) and \\( \\cos x \\) have period \\( 2\\pi \\); \\( \\tan x \\) has period \\( \\pi \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · The unit circle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "a2TrigCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A point on the unit circle at angle theta, with coordinates cosine theta and sine theta",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "a2TrigDataBtn",
          "panelId": "a2TrigDataPanel",
          "descId": "a2TrigDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "a2TrigDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "cos θ and sin θ at common angles",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            { "en": "θ (°)", "ar": null },
            { "en": "cos θ", "ar": null },
            { "en": "sin θ", "ar": null }
          ]
        },
