            "value": "1.047"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "A point on the unit circle is (cos θ, sin θ) — the Reference box's definition, live. Drag θ to 90° and compare the radian readout to Worked example 9.A's π/2.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Unit circle",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Radians",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( 180^{\\circ}=\\pi \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Identity",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sin^{2}\\theta+\\cos^{2}\\theta=1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Period",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( 2\\pi \\) (sin, cos)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Convert \\( 90^{\\circ} \\) to radians.</p>\\[ \\frac{\\pi}{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Proving a trig identity",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Prove that \\(\\dfrac{\\sin2\\theta}{1+\\cos2\\theta}=\\tan\\theta\\).</p>\\[\\text{LHS}=\\frac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{1+(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)}=\\frac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{2\\cos^2\\theta}=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}=\\tan\\theta=\\text{RHS}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find all solutions of \\(2\\cos^2\\theta+\\cos\\theta-1=0\\) for \\(0°\\leq\\theta\\leq360°\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Factor: \\((2\\cos\\theta-1)(\\cos\\theta+1)=0\\Rightarrow\\cos\\theta=\\tfrac{1}{2}\\) or \\(\\cos\\theta=-1\\). Solutions: \\(\\theta=60°,300°,180°\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
